  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Recall the formula of work done in terms of change in volume and pressure, in the case of isobaric process, where pressure is constant,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, now take the idea of ideal gas equation,&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8.31</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>70</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>291</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.&nbsp;</p></blockquote>",
